It is possible for a KRaft replica to send corrupted records to the fetchin=
g replicas in the FETCH response. This is because there is a race between w=
hen the FETCH response gets generated by the KRaft IO thread and when the n=
etwork thread, or linux kernel, reads the byte position in the log segment.

This race can generated corrupted records if the KRaft replica performed a =
truncation after the FETCH response was created but before the network thre=
ad read the bytes from the log segment.

