Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi everyone,

I=E2=80=99d like to propose a KIP to change the data type of log.segment.by=
tes from
int to long, allowing segment sizes beyond the current 2GB limit.

Rationale:

Currently, the maximum segment size is constrained by the int type, capping
it at 2GB. However, with modern hardware=E2=80=94such as large-scale deploy=
ments on
machines with multiple high-capacity disks (e.g., EPYC servers with 4=C3=97=
15TB
drives)=E2=80=94this limitation makes segment sizes inefficiently small. An=
d too
many handles (log, index, metadata). So Increasing the limit to 3=E2=80=934=
GB (or
more) would better align with today=E2=80=99s storage capabilities.

Would love to hear your thoughts before drafting a formal KIP.

Best,

Mikhail Fesenko

