See [https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-932%3A+Queues+fo=
r+Kafka#KIP932:QueuesforKafka-Configuration]

Base on describe

```

The existing consumer configurations apply for share groups with the follow=
ing exceptions:
 * {{auto.offset.reset}} : this is handled by a dynamic group configuration=
 {{share.auto.offset.reset}}=C2=A0
 * {{enable.auto.commit}}=C2=A0 and {{auto.commit.interval.ms}}=C2=A0: shar=
e groups do not support auto-commit
 * {{group.instance.id}}=C2=A0: this concept is not supported by share grou=
ps
 * {{isolation.level}} : this is handled by a dynamic group configuration {=
{share.isolation.level}}=C2=A0
 * {{partition.assignment.strategy}} : share groups do not support client-s=
ide partition assignors
 * {{interceptor.classes}} : interceptors are not supported
 * {{protocol.type}}=C2=A0: this configuration is used to select the group =
protocol used for KafkaConsumer
 * {{session.timeout.ms}}=C2=A0: this is deprecated in KIP-848 and is not s=
upported for share groups
 * {{heartbeat.interval.ms}}=C2=A0: this is deprecated in KIP-848 and is no=
t supported for share groups


```



