Subject: Re: [VOTE] KIP-1111: Enforcing Explicit Naming for Kafka Streams
 Internal Topics
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hey.

Just a note about KIP-1111: We accepted this KIP, and the main
proposal is a new config which optionally treats any implicitly named
internal topic as fatal. However, the KIP also proposes logging a WARN
message about every topic / internal topic that has an auto-generated
name even when the config is off. This will mean a lot of users will
get these warnings starting with 4.1. I personally missed that detail
when discussing the KIP. I just point it out explicitly, since others
may have missed it as well, and it wasn't really discussed. In
retrospect, I would have objected to the WARN log, as any user
starting with a basic Kafka Streams example will be immediately
confronted with them. But it may be that I am the only one who missed
it, in which case I=E2=80=99m okay with going forward with the KIP as
accepted.

Cheers,
Lucas

