Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-18807) Group coordinator under-reports
 thread idle time
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Sean Quah created KAFKA-18807:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Group coordinator under-reports thread idle time
                 Key: KAFKA-18807
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18807
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: group-coordinator
            Reporter: Sean Quah
            Assignee: Sean Quah


When events arrive at the event processor with less than 1/group.coordinator.threads ms between them, the thread idle time is rounded down to 0 because of integer division.

eg. when the group coordinator has 8 threads, and it receives >1k offset commit requests per second evenly split across shards, the thread idle time metric will be under-reported.

https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/2353a7c5081b53402d5092afd255e2bdf7aa2d20/coordinator-common/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/coordinator/common/runtime/MultiThreadedEventProcessor.java#L141



