Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi, Mikhail,

Currently, the index file uses 4 bytes to represent the file position of a
record batch within a segment file. This is based on the assumption that
each segment is capped at 2GB. RemoteLogSegmentMetadata is a public
interface and currently uses int to represent segmentSizeInBytes. If we
want to increase the segment size, we need to consider the impact to those
places too.

Thanks,

Jun

On Thu, Feb 13, 2025 at 1:32=E2=80=AFPM Mikhail Fesenko <proggga@gmail.com>=
 wrote:

> Hi everyone,
>
> I=E2=80=99d like to propose a change the data type of log.segment.bytes f=
rom int to
> long, allowing segment sizes beyond the current 2GB limit.
>
> Rationale:
>
> Currently, the maximum segment size is constrained by the int type, cappi=
ng
> it at 2GB (max int). However, with modern hardware=E2=80=94such as large-=
scale
> deployments on machines with multiple high-capacity disks (e.g., EPYC
> servers with 4=C3=9715TB drives)=E2=80=94this limitation makes segment si=
zes
> inefficiently
> small. And too many handles (log, index, metadata). So Increasing the lim=
it
> to 3=E2=80=934GB (or more) would better align with today=E2=80=99s storag=
e capabilities.
>
> Would love to hear your thoughts !
>
> Best,
>
> Mikhail Fesenko
>

