ead.run(ShutdownableThread.java:136) {code}
 * Manually verified the last offsets of the replicas, and broker 0 is caug=
ht up in the partition.
 * Even after stopping the produce load, the issue persists.
 * Even after removing the /controller node manually (to retrigger election=
), regardless of which broker becomes the controller, the issue persists.

Based on the above, it seems that during the rollback, brokers in migration=
 mode cannot handle the KRaft controllers being removed from the system. Si=
nce broker 0 is caught up in the partition, we suspect that the other broke=
rs (still in migration mode) do not respect the controller state in ZK, and=
 do not report changes in the ISR of the partitions they are leading.

This means that if a replica becomes out of sync in the last restart (e.g. =
due to a slow broker restart), we cannot restart the brokers while ensuring=
 zero downtime.



